<title>DENMARK: FORECAST-East Asiatic profit seen soaring.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-East Asiatic profit seen soaring.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine analysts polled by Reuters in a survey issued on Tuesday foresaw an average 39 percent rise in profits before tax and ordinary items for Danish shipping, graphic and wholesale group East Asiatic(EAC) for 1996.</p>
<p>The company is to release its 1996 results on Thursday March 13.</p>
<p>The panel forecast a 1996 pre-tax and extraordinary items profit of an average 357 million crowns, compared to 216 million crowns in the previous year on 11 percent higher 16.188 billion crown turnover.</p>
<p>EAST ASIATIC</p>
<p>1996 RESULT EXPECTATIONS - NINE ANALYSTS</p>
<p>				   average     high/low	 1995</p>
<p>Net turnover (bln crowns)   16.188    16.500/15.975   14.421</p>
<p>Pre-tax/extra.items</p>
<p>profit (million crowns)	    357	   400/275	  216</p>
<p>Net result (million crowns)	193	   225/155	  271</p>
<p>--Joern Nurkka, Copenhagen newsroom +33969655</p>
